=end markdown


=head1 NAME

markpod - merge Markdown documentation into Perl POD


=head1 SYNOPSIS


 markpod.pl --inplace lib/My/Module.pm
 markpod.pl --extract-markdown lib/My/Module.pm
 markpod.pl --extract-pod lib/My/Module.pm

=head1 EXAMPLES


 # Convert sidecar or embedded Markdown to POD and update the file.
 markpod.pl --inplace bin/foo.pl

 # Extract Markdown to a sidecar file.
 markpod.pl bin/foo.pl --extract-markdown --outfile=bin/foo.pl.md

 # Convert and write the transformed source to STDOUT.
 markpod.pl lib/My/Module.pm

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<markpod.pl> is the command-line interface for C<ExtUtils::Markdown::Pod>. It
processes Perl modules and scripts, finds Markdown documentation, converts that
Markdown to POD, and writes a merged documentation block back into the source.

Markdown can come from a same-path sidecar file such as C<lib/My/Module.pm.md>
or from an embedded POD block beginning with C<=begin markdown>.

The generated output keeps the Markdown source and appends generated POD, so the
file remains editable in Markdown while still working with POD tools such as
C<perldoc>, C<pod2man>, and CPAN metadata extractors.

Status messages are written to STDERR. Converted source, extracted Markdown, and
extracted POD are written to STDOUT unless C<--outfile> is supplied.


=head1 OPTIONS

B<--file|--fn|--f|--in> input file to process. Positional filenames are also
accepted.

B<--inplace> update the file in place

B<--outfile|--output|--o> file to write extracted Markdown, extracted POD, or
transformed source to. Without this option, output goes to STDOUT.

B<--dialect> Markdown dialect passed to C<Markdown::Pod>. The default is
C<GitHub>.

B<--extract-markdown|--extract|--md|--markdown> extract Markdown from the input
file without updating POD.

B<--extract-pod|--pod> extract generated POD from the input file.

B<--nobackup> do not create a C<.bak> file when doing an in-place update.

B<--quiet> suppress status output.

B<--verbose> include additional status messages, such as skipped MakeMaker
targets and backup behavior.

B<--debug> enable developer diagnostics.

B<--help> show help synopsis.

B<--man> show the full manual page.

B<--version> show version information.


=head1 STATUS OUTPUT

Normal status output is intentionally short:


 markpod: lib/My/Module.pm.md -> lib/My/Module.pm: starting merge
 markpod: lib/My/Module.pm: finished, updated pod
Use C<--quiet> to suppress status lines.


=head1 USAGE

Create a Markdown section in POD using the C<=begin markdown> convention:


  =pod
  =begin markdown 
 
  # POD Heading
  Some **Bold** Text
  [Perl Link](http://perl.org)
  Some `code` in this section
 
  =end markdown 
  =cut 
After C<markpod.pl --inplace> runs, the block is rewritten to retain the Markdown
and append generated POD:


  =begin markdown
 
  # POD Heading
  Some **Bold** Text
  [Perl Link](http://perl.org)
  Some `code` in this section
 
  =end markdown
 
  =head1 POD Heading
 
  Some B\<Bold\> Text
  L\<Perl Link|http://perl.org\>
  Some C\<code\> in this section
 
  =cut

